{"id": "EUVD-2026-99011", "enisaUuid": "d6ff3e14-5c23-32f0-a933-63693b98c3ad", "description": "QloApps through 1.7.0 contains a broken access control vulnerability that allows hotel-restricted back-office employees to create room types under unassigned hotels by supplying an arbitrary id_hotel. Attackers can enumerate all hotels via the unfiltered room type form selector and post foreign hotel IDs to AdminProductsController, creating rooms and inventory under other hotels.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T22:32:49", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/SyMoELioMx", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/controllers/admin/AdminProductsController.php#L3038-L3052", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/controllers/admin/AdminProductsController.php#L2362-L2367", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/modules/hotelreservationsystem/classes/HotelBranchInformation.php#L488-L496", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/pull/1649", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/commit/24ff5f5e6ba0c7a42c83ce8155b318c3ef8c915d", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/qloapps-through-1.7.0-authorization-bypass-via-id-hotel-in-room-type-creation"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4pjr-6wp6-x63v", "CVE-2026-110226"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8fac07c8-ff6e-36d4-a69e-bcd11b1d4bc1", "product": {"name": "QloApps", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aa869b82-93be-3a5f-b3c2-5e32596c7eef", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}], "isExploited": false}